                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "What about if there was a new spec: `gen_spec.consecutive_pattern()`. This would take a pattern, similar to current behaviour when you don't use a spec function, but when it attempts to find a covering match, it joins multiple instances of pattern together, perhaps with a 'separator' pattern?",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">What about if there was a new spec: <code class=\"notranslate\">gen_spec.consecutive_pattern()</code>. This would take a pattern, similar to current behaviour when you don't use a spec function, but when it attempts to find a covering match, it joins multiple instances of pattern together, perhaps with a 'separator' pattern?</p>",
                    "bodyText": "What about if there was a new spec: gen_spec.consecutive_pattern(). This would take a pattern, similar to current behaviour when you don't use a spec function, but when it attempts to find a covering match, it joins multiple instances of pattern together, perhaps with a 'separator' pattern?",
